  "answer": "I can't give you an AUD-to-peso rate from my data, because the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) doesn't publish one. Its exchange-rate table covers about 25 currencies, such as the US dollar, euro, yen, yuan and rand, and the Argentine peso isn't one of them.\n\n**What I can give you:** at 4pm AEST on 16 October 2026 (the latest data), **A$1 = US$0.6947**. That's down from US$0.717 on 1 September 2026.\n\n**How to work out the peso rate:** find today's official US dollar to peso rate from Argentina's central bank (BCRA), a bank, or a site like XE or Google. Then multiply:\n\n> ARS per A$1 = 0.6947 × (ARS per US$1)\n\nFor example, if US$1 bought 1,400 pesos, A$1 would buy about 0.6947 × 1,400 ≈ 973 pesos. The 1,400 is just an example, not the actual rate.\n\n**Check which rate you're looking at:** Argentina has had more than one exchange rate. The official rate and the informal \"blue\" dollar rate (which tourists often deal with) have at times been very different. The peso also moves fast, so use a rate from today rather than one that's even a few weeks old.",
